#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate the wolf test fixture packages.

The tests in src/tests/auto read a directory of small packages that the build passes as the
WOLF_TEST_FIXTURES_SOURCE environment variable. Those packages used to be tracked in the repository;
they are generated now, so the repository carries test code rather than package artifacts.

The table below is the single source of the fixture content. It was recorded from the object store
rather than from a working tree, because a Windows checkout rewrites most of those files to CRLF,
and the script writes UTF-8 with line feeds so that the generated bytes match the recorded ones.

Usage:
    python3 scripts/make-test-fixtures.py --output build/test-fixtures
    python3 scripts/make-test-fixtures.py --check build/test-fixtures
    python3 scripts/make-test-fixtures.py --list
"""

